bloub-swift
===========

This repository contains a TypeScript port of the bot-morphing engine from
**bloub** — "An SVG recreation of the x.ai bot avatar", by Jérémy Perret —
<https://github.com/jeremy-prt/bloub>, released under the MIT License.

What is derived from bloub
--------------------------

The engine under `ts/src/`: `engine`, `states`, `cycles`, `shape`, `face`,
`expressions`, `eyefit`, `math`, `decor`, `repere`, and the measured radial
profiles in `profiles.ts`. The structure, the measured constants and the
reasoning recorded in the comments come from that project; the port translates
them to English and drops the Vue layer. `profiles.ts` is measurement data
taken from bloub's reference footage and is copied verbatim, because it cannot
be recomputed without the video.

Its MIT copyright notice is preserved in `LICENSE` above ours.

What is NOT derived from bloub
------------------------------

- `ts/src/identity.ts` — the identity look: seed, draw order, the OKLCH palette
  and the three resting moods.
- `ts/src/skins.ts` — the eight body silhouettes. These replace bloub's
  customiser catalogue; they are built analytically here from the generic
  radial-profile helpers.
- `ts/src/status.ts` — bot status to engine state.
- The golden set in `golden/`.

Original work, MIT, same terms.

Trademarks and look
-------------------

bloub recreates the avatar of x.ai's bot. Neither that avatar nor its look is
licensed, and **this project does not use it**: no x.ai asset, palette or
silhouette is reproduced here. The bodies in `skins.ts` are our own eight
shapes, the palette is generated per bot from an OKLCH hue, and the resting
moods are a subset of the expression catalogue. The resemblance that remains is
that of an engine: a filled silhouette whose blob morphs, with two capsule eyes
on a sphere. That is the part bloub measured and released, and it is what is
credited above.
